cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  How China Will Win the AI War: The Convergence Strategy — A
  Structural Path to AI Dominance
message: If you cite this work, please cite the edition you read.
type: book
authors:
  - family-names: Matsuoka
    given-names: Satoshi
    affiliation: RIKEN Center for Computational Science (R-CCS)
abstract: >-
  A structural analysis arguing that China's position in artificial
  intelligence should be read as the fourth run of an industrial playbook
  that already won the solar photovoltaic, lithium-ion battery, and
  electric-vehicle wars. The book treats the elements of AI separately —
  the model, the compute, the semiconductor, the watt, the data, and
  embodied AI — before recombining them, and states four load-bearing
  propositions with explicit falsification conditions. A living document,
  revised as the underlying industrial and technical facts evolve.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - industrial strategy
  - high-performance computing
  - semiconductors
  - open-weight models
  - AI for science
  - technology policy
